// The same table written with a `for` loop — plus a fourth column (n⁴) to
// show how `put` scales: to add a column you add a value and a separator,
// nothing more. A `for` gathers the three parts of a counted loop —
// initialise, test, advance — onto one line, so the body just does the work.
main() {
    auto n;

    for (n = 1; n <= 8; n = n + 1) {
        put(n, "\t", n * n, "\t", n * n * n, "\t", n * n * n * n, "\n");
    }
}
